Test rg77: -m keeps each comment's whole text, within 72 columns
// run_regression.sh assembles this with -m, compares the .mac with
// rg77_mac_comments.mac.ref, and requires each comment line of the .mac
// to be at most 72 columns wide (a tab ends at a multiple of 8).
100/
// This comment, on a line by itself, is longer than one line of the macro1 source can hold, so it is broken at blanks into as many lines as it needs, none of them wider than 72 columns.
    cla     // a trailing comment starts on its statement's line, after a tab, and goes on well past the width, so the rest of it follows on lines of its own
    hlt     // short
// aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa is one word wider than a line
/*
 * A block comment reaches the .mac too, each of its lines a comment line of its own.
 */
    lac [5      // a constant reference closed by the end of its line keeps its comment, wrapped like any other
here, 0

// This comment, after a blank line, is on a line of its own in the .mac too.
    nop
start 100
